      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Detect Ollama WorkOS sign-in redirects",
        "body": "## Summary\n- detect Ollama `/signin` redirects before attempting usage parsing\n- recognize the current WorkOS AuthKit authorization destination\n- surface expired-session recovery instead of a misleading parser failure\n\n## Proof\n\nDeterministic test run on this branch. The fetcher is exercised through an injected HTTP transport — no network, no credentials, no live account:\n\n```text\n$ swift test --disable-sandbox --filter OllamaUsageFetcherTests\n◇ Test \"recognizes current ollama sign in redirects\" started.\n✔ Test \"recognizes current ollama sign in redirects\" passed\n✔ Test run with 19 tests in 1 suite passed.\n```\n\nWhen `ollama.com/settings` redirects to `/signin` (or to the WorkOS `user_management/authorize` page), the fetcher now throws `invalidCredentials` instead of falling through to a parse failure, so CodexBar can try the next cookie candidate and show sign-in guidance.\n\n## Testing\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter OllamaUsageFetcherTests` (19 passed, including the new redirect-detection case)\n- `swift build` clean",
